Package: isoTensor
Type: Package
Title: Cell-Type-Resolved Isoform Abundance Estimation from Bulk RNA-seq
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Koki", "Tsuyuzaki", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "k.t.the-answer@hotmail.co.jp")
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports:
    stats
Suggests:
    testthat,
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    BiocStyle
Description: isoTensor estimates cell-type-resolved isoform abundance from
    bulk RNA-seq isoform abundance and externally estimated cell type
    fractions. Given a non-negative individual-by-isoform matrix X and a
    non-negative individual-by-cell-type fraction matrix A (estimated by
    reference-based deconvolution tools such as Bisque and kept fixed),
    isoTensor solves the non-negative least squares problem X ~ AB by
    multiplicative updates to obtain the population-level cell-type-by-isoform
    matrix B. Individual-specific cell-type-resolved isoform abundance
    based on non-negative tensor decomposition will be provided in a
    future release.
